From 46f4ca06266fa3d7a4679ac952252235e8134f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:54:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Explain G-code reads a lathe's own words - G98/G99
 feed modes, T0101 tool 1 offset 1, G50 S speed limit

The PRELUDE's explain() had one word table, the mill reading, so a lathe
post that opts in would say G98/G99 are cycle returns, T0101 is tool 101
and G50 S3000 is a plain speed. A post now states its own meanings in
its manifest: explainWords (a text, "" to stay silent, or { said, takes }
for a word explained only beside the value word it folds in) and
explainTool = "station-offset" (Txxyy: tool, then offset). fanuc-lathe
states G98/G99/G50 and the T reading, tormach-lathe the T reading. A
malformed table is refused by name when Explain is on; with Explain off
nothing is read and the programs are byte-identical.

Pinned by explain_lathe.rs (fanuc-lathe posted with Explain on and off).

Fixes #1399

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
